          "locator": "Krīḍā 54.1–16; https://sanskritdocuments.org/doc_purana/gaNeshapurANam2.html",
          "paraphrase": "After Śukla’s meal, Vināyaka plays outside and briefly sleeps. Citizens who prepared meals seek the sage’s son at the Kāśī king’s house; the king says he left while playing. Some disparage the choice of a poor man’s inferior meal over wealthy invitations and challenge the king’s deity claim. Devotees find him sleeping at Śukla’s house: sāttvika people wait silently, while rājasika people urge him to rise before the prepared food becomes stale and criticize Śukla’s poverty. The child, explicitly called Kaśyapa’s son, says the devotional meal fully satisfied him, leaving no strength to step or appetite for another mouthful. The people become disappointed.",
